#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00d1bec1-5f96-5ea9-863e-8f7312c8b526" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b43b95-6b54-5507-9e71-fdcfce468f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534370} {:answer/id #uuid "562ab408-894e-5dbf-aef4-4c0a59f1145d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534438} {:answer/id #uuid "73fc0c4a-8712-5f5a-89bc-7a0b89357dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534516} {:answer/id #uuid "97c8ee38-8b13-5f9e-a76e-7584f65b43cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534603} {:answer/id #uuid "d47e8365-50ab-501c-9600-aa054b401dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73fc0c4a-8712-5f5a-89bc-7a0b89357dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534516} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ebe4757-b367-5836-98de-3d05256c7715" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "813ed141-a0ad-5559-9d01-1e28afeea83d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102954" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b0ed011d85165937593e0cc86439f0d26ab61e703c5c74ac824e10a5cfa4adf.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- Its range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- The graph lies in the first and third quadrants\n\n- The function is increasing throughout its entire domain.\n\n- As $x\\to \\infty $, we have $y\\to \\infty ,$ though it does so slowly\n\n- As $x\\to -\\infty $, we have $y\\to -\\infty ,$ though it does so slowly\n\nOf the given options, only graph IV has all of the above properties. Therefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00d1bec1-5f96-5ea9-863e-8f7312c8b526" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d3d367-ef61-5f0e-b028-76b8d02b1bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534332} {:answer/id #uuid "2505ec9c-7b5f-512f-a7e5-688e8971a739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534343} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3893a0-6fa2-54d0-9dad-5ef0f1f4fa0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534532} {:answer/id #uuid "a21b775b-e252-5062-a83b-24ddc437bd27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534632} {:answer/id #uuid "fc3c2d8b-4741-5de4-bebc-838131f9c433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc3c2d8b-4741-5de4-bebc-838131f9c433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534821} :answer-field/id #uuid "19bb8e3c-21b6-517b-aa91-0a2468777551" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb2d031b-f14f-51f1-86a8-2bb2273a329c" :question/math-academy-id "q-89851" :question/problem "![](images/19/19c55ecaf73ac1c0c8db619e6c43d14f35e50e2321ccae5687b3a1bc6a687563.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- Its range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- The graph lies in the first and third quadrants\n\n- The function is increasing throughout its entire domain\n\n- As $x\\to \\infty $, we have $y\\to \\infty ,$ though it does so slowly\n\n- As $x\\to -\\infty $, we have $y\\to -\\infty ,$ though it does so slowly\n\nOf the given options, only graph I has all of the above properties. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3135b492-14a6-5ccf-9b83-deecba63f7f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5d103d-b016-56a7-843d-168644066425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534358} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc5b7f5-341f-5517-9ff3-798e626c786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534417} {:answer/id #uuid "89cbec0e-d997-5f98-9e31-5a809bd2b76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534563} {:answer/id #uuid "e37c7008-ad00-5155-ba60-4410a81c6120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534769} {:answer/id #uuid "f301abba-55eb-5980-9f33-5bed3c4ff731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f5d103d-b016-56a7-843d-168644066425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534358} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec6ef3f5-a1e6-5276-9762-cc4e0cecbe3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96f2566c-9717-5c2b-9e76-8782952293d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89857" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$\n\nI. The graph of $f(x)$ lies in the second and fourth quadrants\n\nII. The range of $f(x)$ is $y\\in [0,\\infty )$\n\nIII. $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n![](images/ab/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since the graph of $f(x)$ lies in the first and third quadrants\n\n- Statement II is false since the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}]}
